# Deliberate backwards version moves, one "<from> -> <to>" per line.
#
# A version that decreases makes every install on the higher line
# permanently un-updatable, because update checks compare by semver
# precedence. That is a release decision; recording it here is how the
# decision is distinguished from an accident, and check-version.sh fails
# on any backwards move that is not listed.
#
# 0.11.51 -> 0.2.0 (fc9c78f, 2026-09-01): version line reset. Installs on
# any 0.11.x build must be reinstalled by hand; `vak self update` cannot
# cross backwards. See the CHANGELOG's "version line reset" entry.
0.11.51 -> 0.2.0

# ENDED 2026-09-02 at 1.0.0. The 0.2.x line could never take a minor bump —
# 0.3.0 through 0.11.50 were already tagged by the first pass — and every
# install on 0.11.x stayed un-updatable for as long as it ran. 1.0.0 sorts
# above both retired lines, so no entry below is expected to match again;
# they are kept as the record of why the gap exists.
